  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "# Description\n\nIn the right wing, the friends list has some kind of rendering issues where some of the User Card's elements don't show up (e.g. user name/status, world name, instance type/count, join button text) (screenshot #1) until you hover the container element that has the autohiding scrollbar (screenshot #2).\n\nThis only happens on Chromium browsers, different PCs, it's fine on Firefox.\n\n# Tested and broken on:\n\n[PC #1 | Windows 11:]\n\n- Chrome 121.0.6167.140\n\n[PC #2 | Windows 10:]\n\n- Chrome 121.0.6167.140\n\n- Edge 121.0.2277.98\n\n# Reproduce:\n\nHappens every few visits/refreshes on Chromium browsers. Doesn't seem to happen when visiting the page with Dev Tools opened.\n\n# What I found\n\nIt fixes itself when you hover exactly the container element that triggers autohiding scrollbar (screenshot #2).\n\nIt doesn't seem like styling issue, e.g. elements being invisible, or React rendering issue - the content is there in the DOM.\n\nLooks like a browser rendering glitch?",
